WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.129
Good morning, John. It's September 9th, 2011,
and you know what that means: It means that

00:00:03.129 --> 00:00:07.439
we are in the middle of being bombarded by
news stories about what the world is like

00:00:07.439 --> 00:00:11.860
ten years after September 11, 2001. And I
didn't want to make my whole video about that

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:15.480
today, but it's kind of hard not to make at
least some of my video about, "ten years after

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.640
September 11th." So we're gonna start out
with that.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:22.599
Part one: What is the world like ten years
after September 11th? I am ten years older,

00:00:22.599 --> 00:00:25.760
and I can't believe that there are people
watching this video right now who were not

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:29.590
alive when that happened. Oh my God.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:36.080
Second thing about the world after September
11th: No one is ever going to win a war on

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:40.750
terror. The War on Terror is a policy. It
is not a war. You can not win a war against

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:46.130
a noun. You win wars against armies and governments
and other countries. You do not win them against

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:51.540
drugs or violence or terror. Every time someone
on any news show says, "This is what we need

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:56.980
to do to win the war on terror," you know
what I want? I want to vomit... onto their

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:57.980
face.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:02.510
Third thing I've learned since September 11th:
"Terror," not nearly as scary as it sounds,

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:07.250
and that's probably why they call it "terror."
In the last twenty years, in the entire world--this

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:12.940
includes September 11th and all other terrorist
attacks--more people have been killed by lightning

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:17.720
strikes than by terrorists. I am thousands
of times more likely to be killed by a drunk

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:23.340
driver than by a terrorist. So when I said,
"No one is ever going to win a war on terror,"

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:27.980
I don't mean that you'll never be safe from
terror. I mean you're always going to be safe

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:29.820
from terror because you always were.

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:35.380
Moving on! I have a poster, and you don't.
Sorry about that. Uh, you can't have that

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:40.390
one; it's mine, but we're getting them back
in stock hopefully by Monday. You can go dftba.com

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:42.870
and back-order them, and they'll ship as soon
as we have them in the office.

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:46.700
Part three: I have a friend who works for
Blizzard, and he got me a Diablo III beta

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:51.520
key so I'm gonna start playing Diablo III
starting now on my gaming channel. Here is

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:52.520
a small snippet:

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:55.920
So I've got a barbarian here; his name is
Kenneth. And there's some Inferi. I should

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:01.590
mention that this game is bloody and violent
and scary. Musty cellar? That sounds like

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:11.560
a place I have to go. I got superior chest
armor? And I got magic gloves! And I got inferior

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:20.890
pants!? Stump! Eat it, stump! Stumps have
gold! Shoes? Oh, that's exciting I love shoes.

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:24.650
Part four: Another amazing thing that's happening
to me right now... Ze Frank's new website,

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:30.780
star.me, has a mission of the day, and today
your mission is to create music using sounds

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:34.440
that I made with my mouth. You go and there's
a little grid thing and you just click on

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:40.660
it and it makes noises. And all the noises
are noises that I made with my mouth.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.230
Five, I think we're on part five: Another
thing that happened on September 11, 2001

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:46.959
is that They Might Be Giants released their
album, Mink Car. And recently somebody got

00:02:46.959 --> 00:02:50.750
in touch with me and told me that they were
putting together a tribute album that was

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:55.069
just all nerdy musicians covering all of Mink
Car and I covered "Bangs," from Mink Car.

00:02:55.069 --> 00:02:59.180
It's the first track on the album, hah. That
makes me nervous. Many of my favorite nerd

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:04.110
musicians are on the album: Tom Milsom, Molly
Lewis, MC Frontalot, Driftless Pony Club,

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:08.390
Mike Lombardo, me! And you can get a physical
CD now at minkcarcover.com or you can get

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:11.900
it on itunes or bandcamp as well. All proceeds
go to the FDNY Foundation.

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:17.150
And lastly, thing number seven or eight or
four, I have no idea: There are so many great

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:21.120
Nerdfighters on tumblr, and I- Tumblr's kind
of amazing to me because it's just this place

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:26.250
that encourages creation in a really new and
interesting and fun and fascinating way. And

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:31.209
also, follow Eff Yeah Nerdfighters on tumblr
because they find the best things in Nerdfighteria.

00:03:31.209 --> 00:03:36.349
The ever-amazing work of Sharkeye Jones, including
this laser-eyed Pizza John fights pizza monster.

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:40.090
I don't know! It's cool! I don't know why!
And it constantly reminds me that any time

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:45.540
anyone does anything with the letters DFTBA,
no matter how impermanent, there's a chance

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:48.280
that another Nerdfighter will see it, and
it will make their day.

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:52.160
There sure is a lot going on. I'm going to
go to the internet and enjoy it. I hope that

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:53.819
you all do too. John, I will see you on Monday.

